From 1d081f23c4aadeda1d84d8bc2b297088439aa8bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:49:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 378/405] Design check: overlaps of compounds measured solid by
 solid, a failed boolean said, one item, more parts, --design-check

From a room's model (reported on 0.7.9): the members of a frame were
never checked against each other and 70 overlaps went unseen.
- The automatic check ran up to 40 parts only (the room has about 150):
  up to 400 now (Mod/Unified/DesignCheck AutoMaxParts), the overlaps in
  another process as before.
- A shape of many solids (68 brackets) against a post: the boolean failed
  and was taken as no overlap. The solids are measured pair by pair (boxes
  first); what cannot be measured is a warning, not "no problem".
- One item: an App::Part or a group marked so (menu, Ctrl+K) has the
  overlaps of its parts left out (a chair, a welded bed).
- DesignCheck.interferences(doc) and FreeCADCmd model.FCStd
  --design-check [interference]: the same measure from scripts, as JSON,
  exit code 1 on an error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
